{"skill":{"slug":"blucli","displayName":"Blucli"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545301512,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":829,"sha256":"9ee7d09e29bf8c5ab75cd645b9e47330a2e1207f1de0ee15c854c9ebef74cba6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1769,"sha256":"510f57e85bc436b0c1f23656f4b591a36b812b0f27d86c53ca623b2e01c63008","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013573788,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bf9193ffaf93cf6e0d1249c87149e7af03b8c7f134bee985697ebf94e9b1f7d0","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bf9193ffaf93cf6e0d1249c87149e7af03b8c7f134bee985697ebf94e9b1f7d0","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: blucli\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It defines a skill to install and use the `blucli` tool for controlling BluOS players. The installation method specified in `SKILL.md` uses a standard `go install` command to fetch and build the `github.com/steipete/blucli/cmd/blu@latest` module. The instructions provided in `SKILL.md` are solely focused on the usage of the `blu` CLI tool and do not contain any evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, prompt injection attempts against the agent, or obfuscation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159607076},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789013573788},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a small, purpose-aligned wrapper for installing and using a BluOS command-line tool, with a disclosed dependency-install supply-chain caveat.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The environment authority is proportionate for a CLI that discovers and controls local audio devices; there is no artifact evidence of unrelated file access, credential handling, exfiltration, or destructive behavior.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill declares installation of github.com/steipete/blucli/cmd/blu@latest, which is coherent with the purpose but mutable because it is not pinned to a reviewed version or commit.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime guidance is concise and task-scoped, including target selection and a reminder to confirm the target device before changing playback.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence, background service, privilege escalation, tool hijacking, memory writes, or executable script shipped in the skill artifact was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is controlling Bluesound/NAD players with the blu CLI, and the documented commands are limited to discovery, playback, grouping, TuneIn, status, and volume control.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable building and running the upstream blu CLI from its current Go module version. Because the dependency is unpinned, cautious users should review the upstream project or prefer a pinned release before installing.","findings":"[T08] expected: The dependency install is expected for a CLI integration, but using @latest leaves a supply-chain review gap; the artifact does not show a malicious payload or hidden behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013573788}}}}}